@startuml seq-sync-rollback
title sync() - atomic rollback on partial failure

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Consumer" as App
participant "runSync" as Sync
participant "ManagedCrud" as Crud
participant "pushRowToTarget" as Push
participant "deleteRowOnTarget\nrevertRowOnTarget" as Rollback
collections "Target A" as TgtA
collections "Target B\n(unreachable / refusing)" as TgtB
database "Source local Redis" as RedisSrc

note over Sync
  Pre-condition: propagation key already
  delivered on both targets, source local
  has the propagation-key hash. dataRow
  has status="pending" with a fresh plain.
end note

App -> Sync : mgmt.http.sync()
Sync -> Sync : UUID + hash(dataRow.secret + UUID, token)

== Phase C: parallel push, one target refuses ==
Sync -> Push : pushRowToTarget(dataRow, A, hash, signed)
Push -> TgtA : POST /api/internal/hmac
TgtA --> Push : 201 { ok, operation:"create" }
Push --> Sync : { accepted:true, effectiveOperation:"create" }
Sync -> Crud : setDeliveryState(dataRow.id, A, "delivered")

Sync -> Push : pushRowToTarget(dataRow, B, hash, signed)
Push -> TgtB : POST /api/internal/hmac
TgtB --> Push : 4xx / 5xx / network error
Push --> Sync : { accepted:false, reason:"target unreachable" }
Sync -> Crud : setDeliveryState(dataRow.id, B, "errored", reason)

== Detect partial failure -> rollback every accepted target ==
note over Sync
  acceptedTargets = [{A, effectiveOperation:"create"}]
  refusedTargets  = [B]

  Strategy per target:
    - effective "create" -> DELETE
    - effective "update" -> PATCH revert
  (no TTL backup exists for fresh creates,
   so PATCH revert would be a no-op there.)
end note

Sync -> Rollback : deleteRowOnTarget(A, dataRow.clientId, signed)
Rollback -> TgtA : DELETE /api/internal/hmac
TgtA --> Rollback : 201 { ok, operation:"delete" }
Rollback --> Sync : { accepted:true }

note over Sync
  No local rollback: source local Redis
  was never written this sync (the write
  only happens in the all-accepted path).
end note

Sync -> Crud : update(dataRow.id, {\n  status:"error", reason:"B: target unreachable",\n  secret:null, lastSyncedAt:now,\n  attemptCount:row.attemptCount+1\n})

Sync --> App : SyncSummary {\n  rows: { propagated:0, errored:1, processed:1, deleted:0 },\n  perTarget: { A: { delivered:1, refused:0 }, B: { delivered:0, refused:1 } }\n}

note over RedisSrc
  Convergence:
    - Source local: still absent (unchanged).
    - Target A: had nothing -> DELETE was no-op-friendly -> nothing.
    - Target B: had nothing -> nothing.
  Federation back to its pre-sync state.
  Consumer must insert a fresh plain to retry
  (the UUID consumed this sync is burned).
end note

@enduml
